---
source: tests/golden/harness.rs
---
  x `image` takes no argument
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-image/image.kdl:3:1]
 2 | 
 3 | image "argument" {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- the name belongs in the block
 4 |     id "Not An Id"
   `----
  help: `image { id "argument" }` is the machine name, and `name` is the human
        one it derives from when absent

  x `image` declares no `name`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-image/image.kdl:3:1]
 2 | 
 3 | image "argument" {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- no name
 4 |     id "Not An Id"
   `----
  help: `name "Tectonic"` is os-release NAME, which the boot menu and the
        desktop read

  x invalid image name `Not An Id`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-image/image.kdl:3:1]
 2 | 
 3 | image "argument" {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- must be lowercase letters, digits and dashes, starting with a letter
 4 |     id "Not An Id"
   `----
  help: it becomes an image tag, a cache tag and the default hostname, all of
        which restrict it

  x `Not An Id` lists no base
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-image/image.kdl:3:1]
 2 | 
 3 | image "argument" {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- nothing to build on
 4 |     id "Not An Id"
   `----
  help: list a base component, such as `base-image { fedora-bootc { version
        "44" } }`, or define one inline with `base "<image reference>"`
